Everything verified. Now implement. Files:

1. `src/App.tsx` — the profile settings page
2. `src/App.css` — layout styles using `--g-*` tokens

Design:
- Page container: max-width 720px, centered, padding.
- Title: `<Text as="h1" variant="header-2">Настройки профиля</Text>`
- Card 1 "Основная информация": avatar block (Avatar xl, upload/remove buttons, hint), name TextInput, email TextInput.
- Card 2 "Язык и регион": language Select, timezone Select.
- Card 3 "Безопасность": Switch 2FA + description.
- Card 4 "Email-уведомления": 3 checkboxes.
- Footer: Save (view="action") + Cancel (view="normal") + saved message.

Language options: Русский, English, Deutsch, Français, 中文.
Timezone options: a list of common zones — Москва (UTC+3), Калининград, Екатеринбург, Новосибирск, Владивосток, Лондон, Берлин, Нью-Йорк, Токио...

State:
```tsx
interface ProfileForm {
  name: string;
  email: string;
  avatarUrl: string | null;
  language: string[];
  timezone: string[];
  twoFactor: boolean;
  notifications: {product: boolean; alerts: boolean; digest: boolean};
}
```

Avatar upload: hidden file input ref; onChange → FileReader or URL.createObjectURL. Use `URL.createObjectURL(file)`. Remember revoke? For a demo it's fine, but let's do it cleanly: keep object URL.

Validation on save: name non-empty, email regex; show TextInput error props. On success: show saved Text positive + console payload.

Cancel: reset to initial.

Card usage: `<Card className={...}>` — Card type default is 'container', view 'outlined'? Default Card type="container", view="outlined" I believe. I'll pass explicit `view="outlined"`? Hmm, not verified default. CardView probably 'filled' | 'outlined' | 'clear' | 'raised'. Just leave defaults and add padding via className or spacing prop (Card extends BoxProps so `spacing={{p: 6}}` works — verified via Box spacing prop; Card extends Omit<BoxProps<'div'>, 'as'|'onClick'>, so spacing is available).

Field helper:
```tsx
function Field({label, htmlFor, children, hint}: ...) {
  return (
    <Flex direction="column" gap={2}>
      <Text as="label" htmlFor={htmlFor} variant="body-2" color="secondary">{label}</Text>
      {children}
      {hint && <Text variant="caption-2" color="hint">{hint}</Text>}
    </Flex>
  );
}
```

Wait: Text as="label" with htmlFor — TextPropsWithTypedAttrs<'label'> includes htmlFor. Should typecheck.

Section titles: `<Text variant="subheader-2">` or header-1? Sections: "Основная информация" — `<Text variant="header-1">` (20px, weight 600). Page title `header-2` (24px). Wait — header-2 is larger than header-1? From the docs above: header-1: 20px; header-2: 24px. Interesting, inverted. So page title = header-2? The traps doc says page title is `header-1`. Hmm: "header-1: font-size: 20px" and "header-2: 24px". Odd but real. For a page title in many Gravity apps they use `header-1` or `display-1`. I'll use `display-1` (28px) for the page title and `header-1` (20px) for section titles. That's consistent with the variant docs.

Layout width: form fields full width of card; selects width="max"? Select width prop: 'auto' | 'max' | number. Default width behavior — for consistency use `width="max"` to stretch. Hmm, "max" means full width? In uikit Select, width="max" stretches to container. I recall `width="max"` makes it 100%. Yes.

CSS file with classes:
```css
.app {
  min-height: 100vh;
  background: var(--g-color-base-background);
  padding: var(--g-spacing-8) var(--g-spacing-5);
}
.app__container { max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; }
```

Use `cn` from uikit? uikit exports `cn` utility? There's `block` from... uikit exports `block`? Yes, uikit exports `block` (bem-cn). Not sure for 7.43. Skip; plain class names.

Footer buttons bar: sticky? No, keep simple at bottom of form.

Form element: use `<form onSubmit>` with Button type="submit" and Cancel type="button" with onClick reset. Button extends ButtonHTMLAttributes so type works.

Also hidden file input — plain HTML input is fine (it's invisible, not a UI control substituting a Gravity component).

2FA row: Flex justifyContent="space-between" alignItems="center" with Text block (title + description) left and Switch right. Per flex contract: description span gets flex:1 min-width:0; switch flex-shrink:0. ControlLabel could wrap but Flex approach is fine.

Notification checkboxes: Flex direction column gap={2}, each Checkbox size="l" with content.

Icons: Camera for upload button, TrashBin for remove. Import `{Camera, TrashBin}` from '@gravity-ui/icons', render `<Icon data={Camera} size={16}/>` inside `<Button.Icon>`.

Icon import — from uikit: `import {Icon} from '@gravity-ui/uikit'`.

Email validation: simple regex.

Let me also double-check `Flex` props: direction, gap, alignItems, justifyContent — standard in uikit Flex. I'm confident: FlexProps include direction, wrap, justifyContent, alignItems, gap, gapRow, etc. Let me quickly verify to be safe.

